Upgrade procedure for spleen

Source: https://github.com/fcambus/spleen/releases/download/VERSION/spleen-VERSION.tar.gz

The release page publishes only the tarball (GitHub reports its sha256
digest); there is no signify signature.  Record the sha256 when importing.

To upgrade to a new version:

1. Download and extract the tarball to /tmp/spleen/spleen-VERSION
2. Use the vendor-update skill (vendor/spleen, contrib/spleen).  Only the
   files already tracked on the vendor branch are imported: the six
   spleen-*.bdf fonts plus AUTHORS, ChangeLog, LICENSE and README.md.
   The other formats in the tarball (pcf, otf, psfu, woff, ...) and the
   tests, blocks, cp437 and dos directories are not imported.  There is
   no Xlist; the pruning is simply "copy only the tracked files".
3. Check share/vt/fonts: the Makefile converts each spleen-WxH.bdf with
   vtfontcvt, and INDEX.fonts lists the resulting .fnt files.  Add entries
   if upstream adds a new size.
4. Keep the files identical to FreeBSD's contrib/spleen when possible.

Local patches applied on top of upstream:

  None.

Notes:
  - Imported versions: 2.1.0, 2.2.0.
  - Build check: make -C share/vt/fonts, then compare glyph counts with
    vtfontcvt -v for each size.
